== VERIFIED DEFECTS ==

[1] walks.tex:397 vs walks.tex:406 — factor-of-two contradiction.  (VERIFIED IN SOURCE)
    Eq. eq:walk-rec-dou derives
        <k^out> = (1 - sqrt(1 - 4 q_e)) / (2 q_e),
    which is real only for q_e <= q_c = 1/4 (line 397). Seven lines later (406-407):
    "Simulations confirm this picture, with the threshold near q_c ~ 0.5."
    That presents as confirmation a value the algebra forbids. Either the simulation or
    the rate constant is off. Check against vazquez2001.
    Severity: high — an internal contradiction in a headline result.

[2] projects.tex:174 — unjustified inequality.
    The calculation box derives dc/dn = (1-q) c/n  =>  c ~ n^(1-q), hence c/n ~ n^(-q),
    i.e. alpha = q EXACTLY. But eq:proj-cpfrac then asserts
        c/n ~ n^(-alpha(q)),  alpha(q) <= q
    with no justification for the inequality. Simulations quoted inline give
        q = 0.20 -> alpha ~ 0.11   (45% below)
        q = 0.50 -> alpha ~ 0.28   (44% below)
        q = 0.70 -> alpha ~ 0.43   (39% below)
    and line 191 calls these "a little below the simple bound q". They are 30-45% below.
    The mean-field step evidently overestimates, but the chapter never explains why the
    bound is not tight, nor how alpha = q became alpha <= q.
    Severity: high — load-bearing for the vanishing-critical-path claim.

[3] distance.tex:29 — wrong self-description.
    Reads "This closing chapter, following ...", but outlook.tex is the actual closing
    chapter, and ch:distance is referenced from the outlook as one of six settings.
    Severity: low — trivial fix, but visible to any reader.


