== UNDERIVED / LOOSE RESULTS ==

[10] proteins.tex — the claim that link removal makes clustering decay "a little faster
     than 1/k" is asserted, not derived; the box assumes e_i = q_v(k_i - 1) with no loss
     term. The multifractal spectrum eq:dup-moments is quoted "in the manner of kim2002"
     with no intermediate steps.
[11] projects.tex — the percolation section is un-derived. p_c = 1/<k> is imported by
     citation with no calculation box, and the claimed link "the very same local rule ...
     also sets the average degree <k>" is never computed: no formula <k>(q) appears
     anywhere. Also, <k> is defined as mean out-degree, while Molloy-Reed-type thresholds
     use <k^2>/<k>; for gamma = 1/q <= 2 (q >= 1/2) the second moment diverges, so a plain
     1/<k> threshold is questionable. The empirical q in [0.1, 0.5] mostly keeps it safe,
     but the chapter does not address this.
[12] friends.tex — eq:fr-ck derivation is loose. The integration and the elimination of
     k* in favour of k are skipped, so the constant 2 mu_1 arrives with no visible route.
     Relatedly, the amplitude ratio k*_0 / k_0 forced by eq:fr-reduced is needed for
     eq:fr-ck but never determined.
[13] friends.tex — eq:fr-limits asserts gamma(1) = 2, but as u -> 1 the prefactor
     2(1-u)/u -> 0 while the bracket -> infinity. The 0 * infinity resolution giving
     exactly 2 deserves a line and gets none.
[14] distance.tex — the exponential law eq:path-typeII is motivated, not derived. The
     text admits this ("a full account of it remains open"), and the outlook lists it as
     open problem #1. Fine to leave open, but worth flagging as a known hole.
[15] communities.tex — the even-odd alternation in the cycle-length table (odd cycles
     bring communities sooner) is observed but unexplained.


